 The eight follow one exact diagnostic template: "Cannot use '<alias>' as
 a variable name - it's a reserved keyword. '<alias>' is an alternate
 spelling of the reserved keyword '<canonical>'." — matching the
 `ms`/ `milliseconds` and `message`/`text` shapes already recorded at
 KEY-51/KEY-52.

 `docs/check-probes.sh` mechanically re-runs and matches only the FIRST
 of the eight (below, `abs`) — a single program cannot reach the other
 seven diagnostics in one compile, since the compiler stops at its
 first error. The other seven were each hand-run as their own one-line
 program (`a number called <alias> is 1.` / `Print <alias>.`) and their
 outputs recorded verbatim above; this is the retained record for all
 eight, per PROCEDURE.md §4.
